 "reading": "Each interior hash commits to its one-based position (8.2.1, hash_pospair64), so the receipt's index is bound: the same path and signature verify at the entry's index and at no other index tried, except when the path is empty (the entry is itself a peak; the index is then not used at all). The receipt states no log size: there is no size in [index, path], and the signed payload is a peak, which is the same for every log size in the range shown; once the log grows past it, the peak is buried but still a node, and the old receipt still verifies against it. Size, and freshness, come from elsewhere (a signed accumulator, a consistency receipt)."
